<title>FINLAND: FOREIGN OWNERSHIP IN KEMIRA, MERITA UP IN OCTOBER.</title>
<headline>FOREIGN OWNERSHIP IN KEMIRA, MERITA UP IN OCTOBER.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Foreign ownership of Finnish</p>
<p>companies registered in the Central Share Register (OKR) rose to</p>
<p>27.0 percent of shares in issue at end-October from 26.4 percent</p>
<p>at end-September, OKR said in its monthly review.</p>
<p>Thanks to a share issue and the state's sale of shares,</p>
<p>foreign ownership in chemicals group Kemira Oy rose to</p>
<p>22.50 percent from 13.97 percent at end-September.</p>
<p>Foreign ownership in Finland's leading banking group Merita</p>
<p>Oy rose to 20.58 percent in October from 18.74 percent</p>
<p>after buy recommendations by some brokerages following a</p>
<p>road-show by Merita in the United States.</p>
<p>The registration of Swedish Sparbanken Sverige's </p>
<p>25 percent stake in Aktia Bank raised foreign ownership in Aktia</p>
<p>to 31.51 percent at end-October from 7.43 percent a month</p>
<p>earlier.</p>
<p>In the opposite direction, foreign ownership in electronics</p>
<p>components maker Efore Oy (formerly named Finlandia</p>
<p>Interface Oy) fell to 31.78 percent at end-October from 39.61</p>
<p>percent at end-September.</p>
